rm the race is a true tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Ann Wagner (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Ann Wagner seeks another term in a St. Louis-area district that leans Republican by about four points. Fred Wellman, a retired Marine officer and first-time candidate, won the Democratic primary in August but has struggled financially, holding roughly $242,000 to Wagner's $4.2 million. A September poll from a Republican-affiliated firm showed the race at a statistical tie, and some national raters have moved the contest toward Tossup, though most still call it Likely or Lean Republican.\n\nPrediction markets give Wagner about a 73% chance of winning. The combination of district fundamentals, incumbency and money favors her, but the tight polling and mixed expert ratings suggest a closer race than a typical incumbent year in this seat.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2379, "margin": -4.26}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2517, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2424, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2065, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.22, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1903, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2785, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3439, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.3337, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.3474, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.3466, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.3548, "margin": -2.8}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.378, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.2589, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.2958, "margin": -3.0}]}